%U A188115 18857230104,69193592020,254802169904,941383915572,3488574124056,12964318919492,48304257254692,180416963578324
%N A188115 Number of strictly increasing arrangements of n nonzero numbers in -n..n with sum zero.
%H A188115 R. H. Hardin, <a href="/A188115/b188115.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..31</a>
%F A188115 a(n) = Sum_{k=n-floor(((2*n*(n+1)+1)^(1/2)-1)/2)..floor(((2*n*(n+1)+1)^(1/2)-1)/2)} [t^(n*(n+1)/2-k*(k+1))] (Product_{j=1..k}(1-t^(n-k+j))/(1-t^j))^2. - _Tani Akinari_, Nov 05 2026
%F A188115 Conjecture: a(n) ~ sqrt(3) * 4^n / (Pi * n^2). - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 05 2026
%e A188115 Some solutions for n=6:
%e A188115 .-5...-5...-6...-6...-5...-6...-6...-6...-6...-5...-6...-4...-6...-6...-5...-6
%e A188115 .-4...-4...-4...-5...-4...-5...-5...-3...-4...-3...-5...-3...-4...-2...-4...-4
%e A188115 .-1...-1...-2...-1...-2...-4...-3...-2...-1...-1...-1...-1...-2...-1...-2...-1
%e A188115 ..1....1....2....3....2....4....3....2....2....2....2....1....3....1....1....2
%e A188115 ..4....3....4....4....4....5....5....3....3....3....4....2....4....2....4....4
%e A188115 ..5....6....6....5....5....6....6....6....6....4....6....5....5....6....6....5
%t A188115 Table[Sum[SeriesCoefficient[Product[(1 - t^(n - k + j))/(1 - t^j), {j, 1, k}]^2, {t, 0, (n*(n+1)/2 - k*(k+1))}], {k, n - Floor[((2*n*(n + 1) + 1)^(1/2) - 1)/2], Floor[((2*n*(n + 1) + 1)^(1/2) - 1)/2]}], {n, 1, 30}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 05 2026, after _Tani Akinari_ *)
%o A188115 (PARI) a(n)=sum(k=n-floor(((2*n*(n+1)+1)^(1/2)-1)/2),floor(((2*n*(n+1)+1)^(1/2)-1)/2),polcoef((prod(j=1,k,(1-t^(n-k+j))/(1-t^j)))^2,n*(n+1)/2-k*(k+1))) \\ _Tani Akinari_, Nov 05 2026
